WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.950
The first shot went into arms, I believe,

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.130
it was a 90 year old grandmother
in the United Kingdom

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.406
on December 8th.

00:00:16.406 --> 00:00:17.239
All done?

00:00:17.239 --> 00:00:18.072
All done.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:23.740
And then a week later, a nurse in New York

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.690
becomes the first American
person to get vaccinated.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.720
We'd been dealing with the
pandemic for almost a year

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.650
at this point, and it really
felt like this kind of

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.070
moment where, you know, "Holy crap.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.170
Like, this might actually be the beginning

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:39.613
of the end of that."

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.770
And I don't think any of
us realized, at that point,

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:49.770
just how long of a road
it would be from there.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.570
Covid has been resurging even in places

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:56.580
where they thought they
had it nailed down.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:00.730
This is becoming a pandemic
of the unvaccinated.

00:01:00.730 --> 00:01:02.910
It was a desperate situation in India,

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:06.280
rich and poor alike, they
were all equally hit.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.530
There are a lot of mistruths
out there about the vaccines.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.910
You've seen the pictures, all
over the internet of people

00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:15.129
who've had these shots and
now they're magnetized.

00:01:19.494 --> 00:01:22.830
Most of the vaccines were
booked by the rich nations.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.217
Many of the African
leaders later called it

00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:27.217
"vaccine apartheid".

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.780
Over the past year, the
world has been engaged

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.380
in a massive ethic to end
the Covid-19 pandemic,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.410
but a series of daunting
and unpredictable challenges

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.050
have stood in the way.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:42.020
To understand how far we've
come and where we could go

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.210
from here, you have to trace the course

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:46.770
of the vaccination
campaign across the globe,

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.403
country by country, city
by city, shot by shot.

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:54.040
This is humanity's first
year of fighting back

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.403
against Covid-19.

00:02:04.359 --> 00:02:06.950
As the vaccines were becoming available,

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:09.050
we realized that this was going to be

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:12.650
an unprecedented public
health campaign, globally.

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:16.430
Never before have we had a
vaccine that we tried to roll out

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:19.330
simultaneously all across the world,

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:22.730
and we started to realize
that there was not going to be

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.883
the kind of data tracking
that everybody would want.

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.550
During the pandemic, in
2020, there was very poor

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:38.240
availability of data
tracking the actual cases

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.950
of this disease.

00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:42.900
Public health organizations
were not doing a sufficient job

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:45.840
of tracking case numbers,
hospitalizations, deaths,

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.230
and we realized that nobody
was really setting up

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:53.530
to do that for vaccinations, so we decided

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:57.720
that we needed to step in
and tackle that ourselves.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:01.630
This is Bloomberg's
Covid-19 Vaccine Tracker,

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:03.520
where we tracked vaccinations

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:06.163
of the largest vaccination
campaign in history.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:11.080
We put together a team
of people and decided

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.510
that we would just start
counting and trying to figure out

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.473
where were vaccines going?

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:29.070
At the very beginning,

00:03:29.070 --> 00:03:31.510
everybody was basically just
trying to get shots in arms

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.680
as fast as possible.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.280
The drug companies that
were making these vaccines,

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.860
they had really just begun production.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:43.290
They hadn't nailed down their
supply process just yet,

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.130
and we were really just in this period

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:48.250
of not enough vaccines or even close to it

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.110
to meet what the demand was,

00:03:50.110 --> 00:03:52.622
and so people were
desperate for this stuff.

00:03:52.622 --> 00:03:54.020
Today, we're on the verge

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.980
of another American medical miracle.

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:58.650
Together, we will defeat the virus

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.420
and we will soon end the pandemic,

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:04.070
and we will save millions
and millions of lives.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:08.200
Hundreds of thousands of
lives in the United States

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.013
and around the world would be saved,

00:04:12.013 --> 00:04:16.340
people would still be alive
today if our government

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:19.480
had listened to the
science, had told Americans

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.040
the real risk of this virus
and put tools and information

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.980
and clear messaging out to
help people save their lives

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:29.963
and protect themselves
from getting this virus.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.740
As the U.S. vaccine rollout ramps up,

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.423
major logistical issues start to emerge.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.710
The process the Trump
administration had set up

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.370
was sending vaccines to
states and they were sending

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:48.260
kind of an unpredictable number.

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.330
It was far short of
what the states wanted.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.840
Governors were screaming, you know,

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:55.600
we were trying to get
the basic information

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.500
out of the system, but
there was no tracking system

00:04:58.500 --> 00:04:59.533
for vaccines.

00:05:00.403 --> 00:05:01.360
And we don't have good tools

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.790
for tracking data around Covid generally.

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:07.880
A lot of the data collection
that's done is done by CDC.

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.710
CDC's culture is very retrospective.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:14.070
They're accustomed to doing
these very careful analyses

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.830
that are backward looking.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.730
They're based on retrospective data,

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:19.830
so data they collect after the fact.

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:21.870
It's not the kind of
organization that has sort of

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:25.080
a crisis mentality that
you need to put out data,

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.780
even if it's not fully baked.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.640
So this is the shared spreadsheet

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:33.750
for Bloomberg's Vaccine
Tracker that we would enter

00:05:33.750 --> 00:05:37.920
every day with 175 countries,
all the U.S. states

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.040
and Canadian provinces, and the data

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.120
was coming from all over all
sorts of different places,

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:47.200
from social media to reporters
hounding government sources,

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.160
to, you know, a Lieutenant
governor who wanted to post it

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.300
on Twitter every week.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.630
This normally is not
something that journalists

00:05:53.630 --> 00:05:54.463
should have to do.

00:05:54.463 --> 00:05:56.860
This is data that's normally
tracked by governments

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:59.290
and produced in a kind of uniform way,

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.100
but we have never had
a situation like this,

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:06.500
where real-time information
was required to respond

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:07.483
to the pandemic.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:10.550
As more supply becomes available

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.810
in the first weeks of
2021, the U.S. soon hits

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:15.240
an encouraging number.

00:06:16.074 --> 00:06:17.900
More doses of vaccine administered

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:20.950
than total coronavirus cases to date.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.230
I remember we crossed
this milestone early on,

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:24.700
and it felt like this
really helpful moment,

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:26.630
and then you realize like, "Oh my God,

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.610
there's still so much further to go."

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.340
But in other parts of the world,

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.253
the vaccination campaign
has barely even started.

00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:41.790
Brazil was starting to see a second wave

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:45.200
that started kind of in early mid-December

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:48.360
in the northern city of
Manaus, which turned out

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.863
to be one of the great tragedies
of the pandemic in Brazil.

00:06:58.153 --> 00:07:01.960
Bolsonaro, our president,
has been consistent

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.170
in his approach to the pandemic in that

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.873
he has mostly dismissed it.

00:07:17.002 --> 00:07:19.180
He does not believe in vaccines.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:22.110
He just thinks people get better immunity

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:25.470
when they get sick and
recover, and so his government

00:07:25.470 --> 00:07:28.630
was very late in buying vaccines.

00:07:28.630 --> 00:07:31.620
We had a Senate probe into
the government's handling

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:35.840
of the pandemic this year,
that looked at all the attempts

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:38.440
that were made by Pfizer, for example,

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:41.350
in selling vaccines to
Brazil, and they emailed

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.200
and they sent letters, and they offered,

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.610
and they called for meetings

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:46.710
and the government would just not respond.

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:50.400
Pressure built on the government,

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.400
enough that they had to buy vaccines,

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.310
but we took so long to buy the vaccines

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:57.710
that once they decided
to buy, the answer we got

00:07:57.710 --> 00:07:59.540
from companies, they
said, "Well, from July on,

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.850
I can give you the shots you want,

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:02.990
but I don't have them right now

00:08:02.990 --> 00:08:04.440
because I already sold them."

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.490
Brazil's limited supply of
vaccines barely makes a dent

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:11.720
in infection rates, allowing
the pandemic to rage on

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.450
almost unabated for months.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:18.100
When it comes to buying
vaccines, you have to rush.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.180
A lot of the countries that waited

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:24.143
ended up having to wait
longer to get the shots.

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.780
In terms of vaccination, at the beginning

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:34.840
of the year, there were
no prospects as yet

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:38.550
on supply of the vaccines to
Africa and what was available

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:42.001
was being booked by the rich nations.

00:08:42.001 --> 00:08:43.970
So there was a concern
that the poor nations

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:46.770
or low-income nations would not get access

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.123
to these vaccines at all.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:54.110
So Covax was a deliberate initiative

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:57.970
to really ensure that there was access

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:02.750
to the Covid-19 vaccines
equitably among nations.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.930
Covax, founded by the WHO

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:08.050
and other global health
organizations in 2020,

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:11.180
sets an ambitious goal for 2021,

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:13.540
deliver nearly 2 billion vaccine doses

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:16.570
to low-income countries
by the end of the year.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:18.990
It's so important to try
and get these products

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:23.038
into every country and
every environment to stop

00:09:23.038 --> 00:09:26.810
this crisis, save lives
as rapidly as possible.

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:29.580
It's impossible that the
global economy going again,

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.040
unless all countries are vaccinating.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.490
It's impossible to protect

00:09:34.490 --> 00:09:38.090
against the emergence of variants
if we are only vaccinating

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.997
in some parts of the world.

00:09:39.997 --> 00:09:43.430
Key to Covax's supply
is a country long-known

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:46.860
as one of the world's
pharmaceutical powerhouses.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.540
India, of course, is known
as the pharmacy to the world

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.650
because it produces the vast majority

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.100
of the world's vaccines.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:56.130
In fact, much of that is
located just in one institute,

00:09:56.130 --> 00:09:58.710
the Serum Institute of
India on the outskirts

00:09:58.710 --> 00:10:00.033
of the city of Mumbai.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:04.430
The Serum Institute had got
a license to mass produce

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:08.560
doses of the AstraZeneca
vaccine, and it had agreed

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.890
to actually export this
to the Covax initiative,

00:10:11.890 --> 00:10:14.360
and Covax was, of
course, counting on India

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:15.910
to make good on these promises.

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:21.150
Going into 2021, the mood in
India was one of jubilation.

00:10:21.150 --> 00:10:23.420
India was reporting less than 10,000 cases

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:25.420
or roughly around that level.

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:28.090
Prime Minister Modi went
before the World Economic Forum

00:10:28.090 --> 00:10:30.030
in Davos, and actually said that India

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:31.520
had beaten the coronavirus.

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:47.950
Little did both scientists
and policy makers know

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:51.160
that a more potent strain
of the coronavirus,

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:54.810
what we initially knew
as B1617 was brewing

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:56.260
within the Indian population.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:08.040
So in April, in the US,
there was this real shift

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:11.320
in vaccinations where, all of a sudden,

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:14.280
supply was getting a lot more plentiful,

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:15.917
and there was a real sense that, you know,

00:11:15.917 --> 00:11:19.340
we're really going to
be turning this corner.

00:11:19.340 --> 00:11:21.930
At that same time, we also
began to see, you know,

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.660
that there were people out
there who were not interested

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:25.820
in being vaccinated.

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:28.370
Covid-19 vaccines can help save lives,

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:31.330
but many people are still
hesitant to get that jab.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:34.000
It wasn't that long ago that
all we were talking about

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.410
was how hard it is to get

00:11:35.410 --> 00:11:37.580
a Covid-19 vaccination appointment.

00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:38.890
Now, take a look around me.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:40.840
See all these empty chairs.

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.207
If you're like 21 years
old, and you say to me,

00:11:43.207 --> 00:11:44.320
"Should I get vaccinated?"

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:45.510
I go, "No."

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:47.710
Yeah, getting people truthful information

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:51.000
about the vaccines was one
of the most critical things

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.710
we could do.

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:57.110
Unfortunately, there are a
lot of mistruths out there.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.560
More people are dying
from the Covid vaccine

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:00.393
than from Covid.

00:12:00.393 --> 00:12:02.440
There has been people
who've long suspected

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:04.470
that there was some sort of an interface

00:12:04.470 --> 00:12:06.890
between what's being
injected in these shots

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.490
and all of the 5G towers.

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:12.510
I think we didn't do a
good enough job, early on,

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.970
communicating to the public.

00:12:13.970 --> 00:12:15.850
We didn't have public health agencies

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:18.930
speaking about the vaccine,
trying to encourage consumers

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.380
to go out and get vaccinated
when they could get access

00:12:21.380 --> 00:12:23.840
to the vaccine, and that was a mistake.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:27.310
We sort of ceded the
information marketplace

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:30.313
to people who were putting
out a countermessage.

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:33.365
One of the things that we began to notice

00:12:33.365 --> 00:12:34.461
when we really began to look at

00:12:34.461 --> 00:12:36.480
vaccination data in the U.S.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.560
in detail, was that there was

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:42.080
this significant split
emerging, and so you can see

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:45.870
on this county-level map here
where red and orange places

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:48.150
have really low rates of vaccination.

00:12:48.150 --> 00:12:50.600
If you take a look at these
places in orange and red,

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:54.380
like the Mountain West down
here in Louisiana, Arkansas,

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:57.000
and Mississippi, places
in Florida and Michigan,

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.133
a lot of those places are the same places

00:12:59.133 --> 00:13:02.783
that have been very, very
hard hit by the Delta variant.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.550
Levels of vaccine hesitancy
remained relatively high

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.580
in the U.S., but the
phenomenon starts to show up

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.880
in other countries, as well.

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:15.623
An example of that globally
is with China and Russia.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:21.490
China and Russia, very
early on, made the decision

00:13:21.490 --> 00:13:24.760
that they were going to start
administering their vaccines

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:27.820
well before they had been fully tested.

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:30.210
The lasting effect of that decision

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:33.560
is that it really shook
everyone's confidence

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:37.290
in those vaccines, both the
people in China and Russia,

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.660
and also the people who were contracted

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:41.273
to buy their vaccines.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:45.210
You can see the result
particularly in Russia.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:48.180
A lot of the Russian people
are still very suspicious

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:51.853
of the Russian Sputnik
vaccine in particular.

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:06.780
In some ways it's
unfortunate because, overall,

00:14:06.780 --> 00:14:08.963
they're safe and effective vaccines,

00:14:08.963 --> 00:14:12.010
just like a lot of the Western vaccines,

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:13.580
but these are the kinds of decisions

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.580
that public health officials have to make

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.123
in a tough situation, and
sometimes there's no right answer.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.290
Meanwhile, another crisis is brewing,

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.656
the rise of a devastating new variant.

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.950
Delta really reared its head in India

00:14:29.950 --> 00:14:32.400
around March, April 2021.

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:35.190
That was when we saw
the numbers increasing.

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:37.930
Everyone thought we were beyond

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:39.919
the worst of the coronavirus.

00:14:39.919 --> 00:14:42.250
What officials in India called a tsunami

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.910
of coronavirus cases, nearly 1 million

00:14:44.910 --> 00:14:47.300
in the last three days alone.

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:50.480
Now the Indian health care
system, on the best of days,

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:51.720
is inadequate.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:54.330
When Delta started flaring up in India,

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.480
what we saw is that
hospitals were so overflowing

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.701
that even the richest
couldn't access health care.

00:14:59.701 --> 00:15:04.535
We don't have anything available
and patients are dying.

00:15:04.535 --> 00:15:08.140
Hospitals were running out of
basic supplies like oxygen.

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:10.640
We saw crematoriums overflowing.

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.803
It was a desperate situation in India.

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.670
With Delta ripping through its population,

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:20.133
India is forced to make a
decision with global consequences.

00:15:21.194 --> 00:15:23.500
The Serum Institute of India ended up

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:27.090
having to redirect much of its supply

00:15:27.090 --> 00:15:28.742
to its own domestic needs.

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:33.550
We saw India discontinue exports to Covax,

00:15:33.550 --> 00:15:36.197
and that really meant
that African countries,

00:15:36.197 --> 00:15:41.020
at the time, did not have
anywhere else to turn.

00:15:41.020 --> 00:15:44.110
Midway through the year,
Covax has only distributed

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:47.630
88 million doses, far
short of its original goal

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.083
of 1.8 billion by the end of the year.

00:15:51.690 --> 00:15:53.820
We did an analysis of the gap

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:56.820
between the wealthy countries
and the poorest countries

00:15:56.820 --> 00:15:59.670
and their access to these
vaccines, and we found

00:15:59.670 --> 00:16:02.590
that the wealthiest countries
were getting vaccinated

00:16:02.590 --> 00:16:05.300
at a rate that was 25 times faster

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:06.650
than the poorest countries.

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:09.530
And the poorest countries,
they're still struggling

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:12.867
to get basic levels of vaccination

00:16:12.867 --> 00:16:14.816
and the countries are suffering for it.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:20.350
Every time vaccines came,
supplies would be over

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:22.620
in just a matter of hours.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.440
I remember when I tried
to go get my first shot

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:30.920
for the AstraZeneca vaccine,
I waited a whole day

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:34.630
in a queue and I could not
get it, so I only managed

00:16:34.630 --> 00:16:37.759
to get my first shot
after queuing for days.

00:16:37.759 --> 00:16:41.473
It really showed how big that divide is.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.339
The vaccine campaign in the United States

00:16:56.339 --> 00:17:01.150
kind of hit its low point in July 2021,

00:17:01.150 --> 00:17:05.030
and that is largely because
things were going really well

00:17:05.030 --> 00:17:05.863
at that point.

00:17:05.863 --> 00:17:08.090
It was summertime, we celebrated July 4th

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:10.960
as kind of like a turning point.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:14.913
But very swiftly after that
came the Delta mutation.

00:17:17.950 --> 00:17:19.930
The Delta mutation, the vaccine

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.610
is less effective against it.

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:24.630
It still keeps people out of the hospitals

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:28.910
and prevents a lot of deaths,
but people started getting

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:31.760
and spreading and transmitting
the virus more and more.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:34.310
The Delta variant, in
fact, already sending

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:38.310
unvaccinated Americans to the
hospital in alarming numbers.

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:41.742
Our in-patient units are at capacity,

00:17:41.742 --> 00:17:46.742
and so people have to either
get better enough to go home,

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.250
or if they succumb to their illnesses,

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.454
and die, that opens up a bed.

00:17:51.454 --> 00:17:54.400
The Delta variant, because
it is so contagious,

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:57.820
does, unfortunately, a very
good job finding people

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.820
who haven't yet been vaccinated.

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:03.930
Nurses are not only tired,
but in short supply.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:07.030
We have a very low vaccination
rate in our community

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:10.610
here in Idaho, and nobody's masked,

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.690
and people are like, "Yeah."

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:14.298
It's all open, it's all free."

00:18:14.298 --> 00:18:16.681
And it's devastating to me.

00:18:16.681 --> 00:18:18.830
Will the vaccine save them now?

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:21.194
No, but you could have done that before.

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:24.800
Soon after Delta's arrival in the U.S.,

00:18:24.800 --> 00:18:27.810
evidence starts to emerge
that the vaccine's efficacy

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:29.930
is waning over time.

00:18:29.930 --> 00:18:32.580
The problem is first identified in Israel,

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:35.270
one of the world's leaders
in vaccine administration

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:36.410
and data tracking.

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:40.320
You had Israel collecting
more systematic data,

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:41.770
and they were the first to pick that up.

00:18:41.770 --> 00:18:44.700
CDC actually dismissed the Israeli data

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.370
when it first emerged in the summer.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.490
CDC's probably going to do a
really good analysis of that

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:52.740
and tell us exactly how
many breakthrough infections

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:56.470
occurred six months later,
but it doesn't help inform

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.537
decisions that have to get
made in real time, like,

00:18:58.537 --> 00:19:00.720
"Should we be administering boosters

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.258
to high-risk populations?"

00:19:03.924 --> 00:19:06.545
The news is not as bleak in
other parts of the world.

00:19:09.275 --> 00:19:11.924
India's infection rate,
having peaked in May,

00:19:11.924 --> 00:19:15.160
continues to plummet as the
country's vaccination program

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:16.780
finally gathers steam.

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:20.173
Vaccinations increased
sevenfold from April to August.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:23.790
In Brazil, whose anemic early campaign

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.950
cost hundreds of thousands of lives,

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:28.510
a stunning turnaround is underway.

00:19:28.510 --> 00:19:33.510
In June, July, you really
started seeing more of a pickup

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:36.610
and in July that coincides
with when we started getting

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:39.690
more Pfizer shots at hand,

00:19:39.690 --> 00:19:42.930
and when governments
started broadening groups

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:45.200
that were eligible for vaccine.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.530
Brazil's rate of first doses administered

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:49.663
soon surpasses that of the U.S.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:53.700
Relatively low levels of vaccine hesitancy

00:19:53.700 --> 00:19:55.380
helped make this possible.

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:57.880
The country's world-class
national health care system

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.290
also plays a decisive role.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:02.190
It would have been much, much worse

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:06.250
without this public health care
system, which is everywhere.

00:20:06.250 --> 00:20:08.190
Brazil is a huge country.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:12.490
They have more than 30,000
posts spread across the country

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:15.412
so you will see pictures
of health care workers

00:20:15.412 --> 00:20:18.920
giving vaccines in canoes
in the Amazon, you know,

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:21.430
and it really is everywhere.

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:23.730
Yes, we took much longer than needed

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:27.130
to actually start
vaccinating, but right now,

00:20:27.130 --> 00:20:30.068
it is a success story,
Brazil's vaccination campaign,

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:33.947
despite Bolsonaro railing
against vaccines to this day.

00:20:43.457 --> 00:20:46.332
We are just now preaching to people

00:20:46.332 --> 00:20:47.563
and we are praying for people.

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:51.281
Because there's no jab

00:20:51.281 --> 00:20:54.190
and people have become, now
they are resorting to faith.

00:20:55.280 --> 00:21:00.280
The vaccination rates
in Africa are still low.

00:21:00.432 --> 00:21:02.398
Around November,

00:21:02.398 --> 00:21:06.697
we were still looking at around 6%.

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:14.150
The coronavirus has taken
a huge economic toll

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:18.350
that has already taken
back some of the gains

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:21.393
that we achieved as far
as poverty reduction,

00:21:22.820 --> 00:21:26.040
so there's a huge social
and financial toll

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:28.593
that this pandemic has put on Africa.

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:35.170
For many African governments,
it was a rude awakening

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:40.170
of being dependent on others for basics.

00:21:41.120 --> 00:21:45.960
So we have seen several
African leaders announce plans

00:21:45.960 --> 00:21:50.160
to set up vaccination plants.

00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:55.120
South Africa, Senegal,
Rwanda, Uganda, Kenya,

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:58.430
all announced plans to either expand

00:21:58.430 --> 00:22:01.500
or actually start new vaccination plants.

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:04.070
They want to be prepared
for the future so that,

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:07.790
in case of a, say another pandemic,

00:22:07.790 --> 00:22:10.730
then you will not really be solely relying

00:22:10.730 --> 00:22:12.413
on vaccines from outside.

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:16.330
It's been a rude
awakening for the Africans

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:19.113
to shape up for the future.

00:22:32.300 --> 00:22:35.940
As 2021 comes to an end,
the threat of Covid-19

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:38.130
is far from extinguished.

00:22:38.130 --> 00:22:41.430
Even as many countries have
achieved high vaccination rates,

00:22:41.430 --> 00:22:45.000
others lag far behind, and a new variant

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:48.060
of unknown potency has started to spread.

00:22:48.060 --> 00:22:51.140
Omicron is already labeled
a "variant of concern",

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:53.330
meaning it could be more transmissible

00:22:53.330 --> 00:22:56.020
and possibly more virulent.

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:58.570
I think one of the challenges of dealing

00:22:58.570 --> 00:23:02.520
with the SARS-CoV-2
virus is that, you know,

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:06.650
it always takes several weeks
to really get the answers

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:08.770
that you need.

00:23:08.770 --> 00:23:11.450
I don't think we know
yet what the future is

00:23:11.450 --> 00:23:14.850
with Omicron and hopefully
we will in the coming days

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:16.810
and weeks, but I think uncertainty

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:20.470
is probably the core
story of this pandemic,

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:24.090
and having to make decision after decision

00:23:24.090 --> 00:23:26.823
without all of the
information that you need.

00:23:32.310 --> 00:23:37.130
This pandemic has really
highlighted a lot of the problems

00:23:37.130 --> 00:23:40.000
with the global public health system,

00:23:40.000 --> 00:23:43.410
but I think it's also
important to take a step back

00:23:43.410 --> 00:23:47.110
and look at what just happened.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:50.210
A year after the first
shots went into arms,

00:23:50.210 --> 00:23:53.510
8 billion shots have been administered.

00:23:53.510 --> 00:23:55.400
That is a stunning number.

00:23:55.400 --> 00:24:00.033
We have vaccine campaigns in
every country in the world.

00:24:00.950 --> 00:24:02.950
That didn't happen with polio,

00:24:02.950 --> 00:24:05.040
it didn't happen with a smallpox vaccine,

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:08.798
it didn't happen with, you
know, AIDS medications.

00:24:08.798 --> 00:24:10.793
For all of those, it took decades.

00:24:11.800 --> 00:24:14.940
How long this pandemic persists depends,

00:24:14.940 --> 00:24:17.610
to the largest degree, on
how we use the knowledge

00:24:17.610 --> 00:24:19.770
we've gained so far and the tools

00:24:19.770 --> 00:24:22.010
that are becoming available
in terms of vaccines,

00:24:22.010 --> 00:24:23.700
tests and treatments.

00:24:23.700 --> 00:24:26.550
We could have this
pandemic well under control

00:24:26.550 --> 00:24:29.550
and be coming out the other
side of it within six months,

00:24:29.550 --> 00:24:32.130
or it could take over a year.

00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:35.170
We've got to make sure that the
tools that we have available

00:24:35.170 --> 00:24:38.200
are equitably distributed around the world

00:24:38.200 --> 00:24:41.180
so that we can reduce the
risk of variant emergence

00:24:41.180 --> 00:24:44.910
as we bring down the burden
of disease and, of course,

00:24:44.910 --> 00:24:46.913
get economies functioning again.

